think Last lap shipped image/compose.rye (paint_over, paint_over_region) -- the compositing verb. The natural next rung composes that verb: paint_tiled paves a box with copies of a small source pattern, the CSS background-repeat gesture (a texture, a wallpaper, a motif that fills a panel). Genuine surface need, small, adds not even a new pixel loop -- it routes each tile to compose.paint_over_region.
think Design: paint_tiled(target,x,y,w,h,pattern) tiles from the corner; a boundary tile the pattern size does not divide is CLIPPED to the box edge (ceiling-division tile count, min(pw, w-lo_x) window), exactly as checker_paint clips a boundary cell. A pattern larger than the box is itself clipped -- the same code path, no special case.
think Compose not braid held: compose.paint_over_region OWNS the blit, qoi owns both buffers, this rung only routes each tile to its window and its clip. Compose IS the crux word, and this rung honors it by composing compose itself.
think Council rota lap 15 (15 mod 27) -> context/TAME_CORE.md (with TAME_GUIDANCE). Applied: bound everything (the box checked once up front in u64), assert invariants first (>=2 positive asserts per fn), say why (each clip and ceiling division carries its reason). The tile count is a ceiling division so a boundary tile is clipped not dropped.
obs GREEN on the first build and first witness run, no reds. One tidy caught before build: I initially added an unused green/blue binding plus a bogus silence line; removed both so the selftest declares only the colors it checks (red, black, white) -- TAME clean, no dead bindings.
obs The single-sprite render from last lap and the tile render this lap together give a surface both gestures the McMaster-Carr trick needs: draw one indexed tile, or pave a whole area with a repeating motif.
